cdex (0.0.4-1cd) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Ship the ReactOS Marlett.ttf font in usr/share/cusdeb/cdex/fonts/ and
    symlink it into the Wine prefix at C:\windows\Fonts. The ReactOS shell
    draws Start Menu submenu arrows and other frame controls via Marlett
    glyphs; without the ReactOS font Wine's built-in Marlett renders glyph
    '8' as a thin "×" instead of a right-pointing arrow.

 -- Artem Lavrukhin <lavryha4590@gmail.com>  Thu, 20 Aug 2026 18:20:51 +0300

cdex (0.0.3-2cd) trixie; urgency=medium

  * cdex-win32-session: stop trying to recreate the reactos-explorer.exe
    symlink on every login. /usr/share/cusdeb/cdex is root-owned, so the
    ln -sf there silently failed with "Permission denied" on every
    session start (masked because it ran as an `if` condition under
    set -e); it was also redundant, since the symlink is already
    shipped by the package.
  * Ship that symlink via debian/cdex-base.links (dh_link) instead of a
    plain ln -sf in the Makefile install rule. The previous approach
    already produced a correctly dpkg-owned symlink (fixed in
    0.0.1-5cd), so this is a packaging-style cleanup, not a fix for an
    unowned file.

 -- Artem Lavrukhin <lavryha4590@gmail.com>  Wed, 19 Aug 2026 20:50:55 +0300

cdex (0.0.3-1cd) trixie; urgency=medium

  * add the CusDeb brand wallpaper: the PNG master lives in
    wallpapers/cusdeb-race.png and is converted to BMP at package build
    time (the desktop paint path loads the wallpaper via LoadImageW,
    which only supports BMP); installed to
    usr/share/cusdeb/cdex/Web/Wallpaper/, following the Web\Wallpaper\
    convention used by Windows.
  * cdex-registry: set the new wallpaper as the default desktop
    background (Wallpaper, WallpaperStyle, TileWallpaper) and drop the
    custom #5D81AB background-color setup (Control Panel\Colors\Background
    and the CustomColors palette entry), so that only the wallpaper is
    installed by default.
  * cdex-registry: also set HKLM\...\CurrentVersion\WallPaperDir to
    C:\reactos\Web\Wallpaper (wine.inf never creates it), so that desk.cpl
    scans the wallpaper directory when filling its background list.
  * recolor the remaining #5D81AB brand backgrounds (the lightdm greeter
    and the xsetroot X root color) to #74A7E2 to match the main
    background of the new wallpaper.

 -- Evgeny Golyshev <eugulixes@cusdeb.com>  Tue, 18 Aug 2026 18:59:59 +0300

cdex (0.0.2-1cd) trixie; urgency=medium

  * cdex-taskbar-bridge: minimize a window when its taskbar button is
    clicked while the window is active (standard taskbar toggle);
    previously the click always activated the window, doing nothing for
    an already-focused one. The last active task window is tracked on
    each poll, since a taskbar click moves X activation to the taskbar
    dock before the command arrives.
  * cdex-taskbar-bridge: re-assert activation when focusing a window if
    it did not stick; the taskbar (or Wine on unminimize) can steal the
    focus back, leaving a restored window unfocused.
  * cdex-taskbar-bridge: poll the control/launch files every 0.1 s
    between window list syncs (still 0.5 s), cutting taskbar click
    latency from up to 0.5 s to ~0.1 s at ~1% CPU.
  * cdex-taskbar-bridge: don't let a missing _NET_WM_NAME clobber the
    WM_NAME fallback, which hid windows without it (e.g. xterm) from
    the taskbar.

 -- Artem Lavrukhin <lavryha4590@gmail.com>  Wed, 12 Aug 2026 16:30:42 +0300

cdex (0.0.1-5cd) trixie; urgency=medium

  * cdex-calc.postrm, mspaint.postrm, spider.postrm, winmine.postrm:
    guard the cdex-shortcut-helper call. It is installed by cdex-base,
    and "Depends: cdex-base" does not guarantee it is still present
    across separate remove/purge transactions, so the unguarded call
    could fail under set -e and leave dpkg --purge in a broken state.
  * Stop creating reactos-explorer.exe in cdex-base.postinst, where it
    was never tracked by cdex-base.install and never cleaned up on
    purge. Its target is constant and known at build time, so it is
    now created during install and owned by dpkg like any other file.

 -- Evgeny Golyshev <eugulixes@cusdeb.com>  Tue, 11 Aug 2026 18:19:09 +0300

